PUBLIC RESPONSE: {I remain persuaded by the case for B. Several colleagues have already noted that placing the origin near lac with counterclockwise transfer positions azi as an early-entering marker while still leaving a substantial arc of the chromosome between azi and the next commonly scored loci (ton, pro, thr). This geometry produces exactly the prolonged early expression window described in the experiment. 

In contrast, an origin near ton (option A) would require the integration polarity to send transfer directly into azi first, but that same configuration also places ton and the thr-leu cluster immediately downstream; the resulting temporal clustering of early markers contradicts the “before others” phrasing, which implies a uniquely long gap after azi. The counterclockwise-lac geometry avoids that clustering because the next markers after azi lie on the far side of the circle. 

Colleagues favoring A correctly recall the thr–leu–azi–ton order, yet the decisive datum is the length of the post-azi interval rather than simple adjacency. Counterclockwise mobilization from lac satisfies both the early arrival of azi and the extended delay to all remaining markers, matching the kinetics reported for this Hfr strain.}

16.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {I remain persuaded that B is the best fit. The time-of-entry data show azi^s appearing well ahead of the other scored markers with a noticeably extended interval before the next ones arrive. Placing the integration site near lac and driving transfer counterclockwise sends azi into the recipient early while the remainder of the chromosome (ton, pro, thr, etc.) follows only after a long arc; that geometry produces precisely the prolonged early expression reported.  

Several A arguments assume a fixed “clockwise from ton” polarity, yet the classic literature already contains documented discrepancies in how different labs label the circular map’s increasing-minute direction. Once those labeling conventions are allowed to vary, an origin near ton no longer guarantees azi as the unique proximal marker, weakening the case for A relative to the lac-origin counterclockwise configuration. The same convention uncertainty also undercuts the D claims that rely on thr as the leading end.  

Thus the kinetics align most cleanly with B.}

