The repeated claim that only a ton origin with clockwise polarity satisfies the data rests on an unexamined assumption about map polarity. Several colleagues invoke “increasing minutes counterclockwise,” while others treat the same markers as increasing clockwise; those two conventions are mutually inconsistent, yet both are used to justify choice A. Once that polarity ambiguity is acknowledged, the lac–counterclockwise geometry becomes equally (or more) compatible with an early, isolated azi entry. The other listed origins either place azi farther downstream or require the opposite polarity, producing clustered rather than prolonged entry times.  

Thus the time-of-entry kinetics continue to favor B over the alternatives.}

